---
description: Global architecture rules for the GamiAI monorepo
alwaysApply: true
---

This is a monorepo with two independent codebases that never import each other:
- flutter_app/ (Dart/Flutter)
- backend/ (Python/FastAPI)

They communicate ONLY over HTTP, contract defined in docs/api/openapi.yaml.
Never suggest importing backend code from Flutter or vice versa.

Before finishing any task, run `make verify` (or the scoped
`make verify-flutter` / `make verify-backend`) and fix failures.
Never mark a task done with a failing verify_architecture script.

Do not add new top-level folders, rename existing ones, or restructure
package/module boundaries without being explicitly asked to.

When a rule here conflicts with a shortcut that would "just work" faster,
follow the rule. These constraints exist because this is a long-lived,
multi-developer-eventually, production system — not a prototype.
